-- the-rescue-company-muckleneuk (researched)
UPDATE businesses SET description = 'The Rescue Company, based in Nieuw Muckleneuk, Pretoria, provides business rescue, informal turnaround management and consultation services for companies and close corporations experiencing financial distress. Business rescue is a formal process available under South African company law for entities in financial distress, while informal turnaround management instead seeks an out-of-court settlement between a company and its creditors aimed at reducing its overall indebtedness without going through formal proceedings. The company also offers consultation services, advising clients on whether business rescue or liquidation is the more appropriate path given their circumstances. It defines financial distress in line with the Companies Act as a situation where a company appears reasonably unlikely to pay all its debts as they fall due within the next six months, or appears reasonably likely to become insolvent within that period. The Rescue Company points to warning signs such as ongoing cashflow shortages, difficulty paying or negotiating with creditors, reduced demand for a company''s products or services, staff retrenchments, an overdraft running at capacity, and management or ownership disputes causing financial losses, as indicators that a business should seek this kind of help.', source_urls = json_insert(CASE WHEN json_valid(source_urls) AND json_type(source_urls) = 'array' THEN source_urls ELSE '[]' END, '$[#]', 'https://therescuecompany.co.za/'), description_enriched_at = datetime('now') WHERE slug = 'the-rescue-company-muckleneuk' AND description = 'The Rescue Company provides business rescue, informal turnaround management and consultation services to help financially distressed small and medium enterprises restructure debt and avoid liquidation.' AND description_enriched_at IS NULL AND length(COALESCE(description, '')) < 700
